            <ArticleTitle>Ganglioneuroma of small bowel mesentery presenting as acute abdomen.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>573-5</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Ganglioneuroma is a rare benign tumor, usually seen in children and young adults, arising in the central nervous system. Ganglioneuroma of the mesentery is extremely rare; only one case has been recorded. We report the second case of a primary mesentery ganglioneuroma. The patient underwent surgical intervention for diagnostic and therapeutic purposes.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
